# Code owners. GitHub requests a review from the owner(s) of any path a PR
# touches. This only becomes a MERGE REQUIREMENT once branch protection on
# `main` has "Require review from Code Owners" turned on
# (Settings -> Rules -> the `protect-main` ruleset).
#
# One owner today (@BernardoJose90). When a GitHub team exists, replace it
# with @<org>/<team> — ideally a security-minded reviewer for the entries
# below, since a bad change to any of them widens blast radius rather than
# just breaking a build.
#
# Ordering: later patterns win, so broad rules are listed first and narrow
# overrides last.

# --- CI/CD pipeline, OIDC trust, IAM, security scanning ---
/.github/                             @BernardoJose90
/modules/github-oidc-roles/           @BernardoJose90
/modules/terraform-deploy-boundary/   @BernardoJose90
/member-accounts/security/            @BernardoJose90
/.checkov.yaml                        @BernardoJose90
/.tflint.hcl                          @BernardoJose90
/.pre-commit-config.yaml              @BernardoJose90

# --- AI CI failure diagnosis ---
# These control what the LLM agent is allowed to do (`--tools`, `--max-turns`,
# the auth model) and its prompt-injection guardrails. A change here can turn
# "posts a misleading comment" into "has a shell in CI". Review as a security
# change, not as docs.
/.github/workflows/diagnose.yml        @BernardoJose90
/.github/workflows/diagnose-apply.yml  @BernardoJose90
/prompts/                             @BernardoJose90
